<p>However, with our initial algorithm, we=E2=80=99d need to restart the se=
arch entirely to find "bytes." This is quite inefficient. What we want is a=
 data structure that allows us to efficiently search words with shared pref=
ixes, allowing us to find multiple words without restarting the search for =
each of them. This is where the <strong>trie</strong> data structure comes =
into play, as it is excellent for managing prefixes.</p>
<p>Let's begin creating the trie by inserting each word from the provided w=
ords array:</p>
